   "hypothesis": "Closest prior methods: the published full block Attention Residuals with Canon-A/B/C/D (AttnRes-Canon; Allen-Zhu, arXiv:2512.17351), and Engram, Conditional Memory via Scalable Lookup (Cheng et al., arXiv:2601.07372). Difference: retain the 23-layer AttnRes-Canon trunk and add two independently hashed causal n-gram embedding tables, one bigram and one trigram, as additive components of the embedding depth source with learned scalar gains. This uses the unconstrained parameter budget to offload repeated local lexical reconstruction at very small arithmetic cost. Unlike Engram, there is no contextual key/value projection or separate retrieval module. All tables initialize from scratch in the native value-embedding group; training, loss, data, schedule, and optimizer are unchanged."
  },
