   },
   "hypothesis": "Closest priors: full block Attention Residuals with Canon-A/B/C/D (the published AttnRes-Canon; Allen-Zhu, arXiv:2512.17351), and Root Mean Square Layer Normalization (Zhang and Sennrich, arXiv:1910.07467). Difference: keep the 23-layer architecture and parameters, but define every model-path RMS normalization with explicit epsilon 1e-6 and FP32 accumulation, returning BF16 activations. The reference uses a dtype-dependent default epsilon. Since depth mixtures can be small in magnitude, an explicit small epsilon may preserve their rescaling invariance and avoid attenuation during learning. This is a change to the model normalization function only; optimizer, data, training schedule, and LM objective remain unchanged."
  }
